    {
      "slot": "changes-rules",
      "tier": "official_act",
      "text": "In a governing coalition, raised the minimum wage by about 8 percent for 2026 and a further 5 percent for 2027 by regulation, as a commission of employers and unions recommended. The government said more than 6 million workers benefit, about 13 percent of people in work.",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/aktuelles/mindestlohn-steigt-2391010",
        "https://www.zdfheute.de/wirtschaft/erwerbstaetigkeit-stagniert-2025-100.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "slot": "seeks",
      "tier": "official_act",
      "text": "In a governing coalition, approved a bill that would let employers offer fixed-term contracts without a stated reason for up to four years instead of two, and make it easier to end the employment of the highest earners, those paid above about 3 times the average wage, in exchange for severance.",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/aktuelles/arbeitsrechtspaket-kabinett-2461564",
        "https://www.oecd.org/ctp/tax-policy/personal-income-tax-rates-explanatory-annex.pdf",
